From 254150eee5f71de70b8cb01c52dfcd3275fd50d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yichao Yu <yyc1992@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:43:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/21] luksan: use DGER for the rank-one update MXDCMU

With an external BLAS/LAPACK, do the rank-one update of the stored
matrix of VAR1/VAR2 (MXDCMU, used while the limited-memory history is
filled and for the VAR1 updates afterwards) with DGER.  On x86-64, where
the loop is compiled for the baseline instruction set, single-threaded
OpenBLAS DGER is 1.1-1.9x faster than the loop for this update; on
aarch64 the two are equally fast.  The rank-two update MXDCMV is left as
a loop: as two DGERs it reads the n-by-m matrix twice, which made it up
to 1.5x slower (1.8x on aarch64) for n >= 10000, and as one DGEMM with
k = 2 it was slower still.

The rounding can change with BLAS, so results differ in the last bits.
With a cheap objective, the time per evaluation of VAR1/VAR2 drops by
1.03-1.11x for n = 1000; for larger n the update is a small part of the
time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/algs/luksan/mssubs.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/algs/luksan/mssubs.c b/src/algs/luksan/mssubs.c
index db1ae90..7b497b2 100644
--- a/src/algs/luksan/mssubs.c
+++ b/src/algs/luksan/mssubs.c
@@ -228,6 +228,14 @@ void luksan_mxdcmu__(int *n, int *m, double *a,
     --a;
 
     /* Function Body */
+#ifdef NLOPT_HAVE_BLAS
+    (void) i__1; (void) i__2; (void) i__; (void) j; (void) k; (void) temp;
+    {
+	blas_int nn = *n, mm = *m, one = 1;
+	if (mm > 0 && nn > 0)
+	    NLOPT_BLAS(dger)(&nn, &mm, alf, &x[1], &one, &y[1], &one, &a[1], &nn);
+    }
+#else
     k = 0;
     i__1 = *m;
     for (j = 1; j <= i__1; ++j) {
@@ -240,6 +248,7 @@ void luksan_mxdcmu__(int *n, int *m, double *a,
 	k += *n;
 /* L2: */
     }
+#endif
     return;
 } /* luksan_mxdcmu__ */
 
